## DoD Canon Gate Evaluation

**Canon discovery:** `docs/DOD.md` found at repo root (`/tmp/tmp.4K7ReBeH0U/docs/DOD.md`). Canon is present, so the DoD Canon Check on Completion Claims section applies (not the "canon absent" fallback).

**1. Malformed-canon check:** Structural elements all present and each ruling line matches one of the three valid forms (`ALWAYS` / `CONDITIONAL | trigger:` / `N/A | category:`):
- `Stamp: v1` — present, parseable.
- `Content-hash: sha256:9cb6f6ddc3ba353d9c50fe691081d2bfdbc0632aaa0de9d55a2b8162dee04c0e` — present, well-formed (64 lowercase hex chars).
- 4 ruling lines (`coverage`, `lint-format-static-analysis`, `mutation-testing`, `visual-regression`), each conforms to one of the three closed forms.

Not malformed. Proceeding.

**2. Hash check:** Recomputed SHA-256 over the byte range defined in `DOD_TEMPLATE.md` Section A.4 (file bytes from offset 0 through the newline ending the line before the `Content-hash:` line):

```
